msgid "Environment variable: ``MM_EMAILSETTINGS_MAXNOTIFICATIONSPERCHANNEL``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/push-notification-server-configuration-settings.rst:132
msgid ""
"We recommend increasing this value a little at a time, monitoring system "
"health by tracking :doc:`performance monitoring metrics </administration-"
"guide/scale/deploy-prometheus-grafana-for-performance-monitoring>`, and "
"only increasing this value if large channels have restricted permissions "
"controlling who can post to the channel, such as a :ref:`read-only "
"channel <administration-guide/onboard/advanced-permissions:read-only "
"channels>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/push-notification-server-configuration-settings.rst:133
msgid ""
"Reducing this configuration setting value to **10** in larger deployments"
" may improve server performance in the following areas:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/push-notification-server-configuration-settings.rst:135
msgid ""
"**Reduced Load on Notification System**: Each notification generates a "
"certain amount of computational and network load. By limiting the number "
"of notifications per channel, the system processes fewer notifications, "
"thereby reducing the load on servers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/push-notification-server-configuration-settings.rst:136
msgid ""
"**Database Efficiency**: Notifications are typically stored in a "
"database. Fewer notifications mean less frequent database writes and "
"reads, leading to quicker database operations and reduced latency."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/push-notification-server-configuration-settings.rst:137
msgid ""
"**Minimized Client Processing**: Users' clients (e.g., desktop and mobile"
" apps) have to fetch and process notifications. With fewer notifications,"
" clients can operate more efficiently, reducing memory and CPU usage on "
"users' devices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/push-notification-server-configuration-settings.rst:138
msgid ""
"**Improved User Experience**: An overload of notifications can lead to "
"performance lags and a cluttered experience for users. Limiting the "
"number ensures that users receive only the most important notifications, "
"which can enhance usability and response times."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/push-notification-server-configuration-settings.rst:139
msgid ""
"**Network Bandwidth**: High numbers of notifications can consume a lot of"
" bandwidth, particularly if they are being sent to many users. Fewer "
"notifications can lead to lower overall network usage and potentially "
"faster delivery of critical messages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/push-notification-server-configuration-settings.rst:140
msgid ""
"**Server Load Balancing**: By reducing the number of notifications, the "
"workload can be more evenly distributed across the servers, leading to "
"better load balancing and preventing any single server from becoming a "
"bottleneck."
msgstr ""

